WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.320
Willow, long ago in a time of magic and sorcery, an evil sorceress named Queen Bavmorda ruled

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.400
the land under a reign of terror.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:33.720
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.720
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.220
And I'm Joe.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.060
Guys, we've made it.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.440
It's the last game of 1989.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.400
That's actually incredible.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.120
How long have we been in 1989?

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.060
We've been here for a long time.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.280
We started in on like January of 2021.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.920
Wow. So it's been about two years.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:01.100
I've already had kids, put them through college.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.500
It's been a long time here.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.420
Yeah. Joe, what was your question?

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.580
What was our next longest year?

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.620
I feel like we haven't even come close to this long.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:15.720
Yeah, no, it's always just getting progressively longer and sad news next year, 1990 is even longer.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:22.900
So these best of episodes that are always how we end each season are only going to get increasingly further away.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:28.600
But funny enough, it's not the number of episodes or rather number of games we played this year.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:37.320
That's interesting. It's that we're ending 1989 and it's exactly the 250th NES game being released.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.060
That's not like on purpose, right?

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.520
Like that's just a fun coincidence.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:47.460
I mean, I don't think there's any significance to the number 250 after what, four years?

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.420
So I think that's just you and your numerology, Mike.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:59.780
Right. Like Nintendo wasn't like, well, we have to release 250 games by 1989 and then we can just put all the games into syndication.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.280
Right. That's what it is.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:06.000
Yeah. And then all the actors who played all the sprites get their royalties.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:06.860
Yeah, they get the royalties.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.220
Yeah. Very funny, Joe.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:18.820
