00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:34.300
But it would have been on right to play, you know, to watch the movie and then find out there's the video game.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.660
And it's a completely tangential story.

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:44.700
I guess the most surprising part of that is just that it seems to be a much more story focused video game.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:50.640
So the fact that it kind of skirts around it as much as it does is like that makes it weird.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:55.900
Because we played a lot of video games based on movies that have nothing to do with the movie.

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:58.380
But they're just like, here, shoot the thing.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:07.640
Right. Well, I would say, though, that this this game, if I mean, again, I can't even confirm how the how much it skirts away from.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:08.860
From the actual plot of the movie.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.320
But but it seems like it does quite a bit.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:17.620
And I think that that is a almost exclusively a positive thing for this game.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:22.080
It never felt like it was taught you're doing some arbitrary thing because it happened in the movie.

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:24.620
It felt like this game was built to be a video game.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:37.920
Like it felt like they did it the right way where they they based it on like the source of the story rather than like, let's take the movie and translate it directly into a video game or like the opposite where it's like, let's just take the characters and make them do shit.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:41.320
That is fun. It's like got a nice balance of like the story.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:46.540
I'm assuming at least the like the heart and the base of the story is there.

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.800
But they didn't feel married to it all.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:54.280
And they like it seems like they decided they decided let's design a good video game and not just design a copy of the movie.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.020
I think that's a great point, Joe.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:59.660
And I was also just checking, you know, the movie came out a year ago.

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:10.800
So it's not even that the movie in the game came out around the same time and that they just were given like a log line and maybe some like like a deck that showed like who these are the characters and these are their bios.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:12.740
It was it was already released.

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:20.380
And so, you know, I don't know what video game timelines were like back then, but it wasn't, you know, the seven year timelines that some AAA games deal with now.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:27.160
So it is it is a little strange, but I, you know, having played the game and having the hindsight behind it.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:39.780
Yeah, I do think that it's for the best that there's no tie into the movie because I understood at all times in this game what I was doing and where I, you know, like what my task was.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:44.480
And if I got lost, it was more, you know, you just don't you don't have access to a map.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:49.460
So you just got to kind of like explore for a little bit, but it's really hard to get like lost lost in this game.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:50.580
Would you agree with that?

00:06:52.080 --> 00:07:06.460
I think there's enough there's enough landmarks and like the directional objectives, like the people in the game are pretty good about like, hey, this is where this might be.

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:07.920
Nudge, nudge, wink, wink.

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:11.300
And you can kind of get a mental map in your head pretty good.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:18.080
So, no, I think that the exploration in this game is is is pretty clear.

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:34.040
Yeah, I'll come right out the gate and say one thing that I noticed about this game that I don't think I've really noticed about any other games is what games of this style where you're on this kind of like long adventure is that this is the first time that I've felt almost no need at all to ever look at a guide.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:44.500
Like, and I think that that has to do with like, yeah, what you're saying, like the world isn't the world is designed to feel big and vast, but it also does not feel super confusing.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:47.240
You don't feel like you can get like super lost it like it.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:51.590
It feels like you're guiding yourself, but also it never it never seems messy.

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:21.570
Okay, yeah.

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:24.270
And then you're going to be like, yeah, I think that's the first time that you're going to be able to do with the game where you just feel like you don't know what to do next.

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:26.530
In those games, you're not really progressing.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.050
You're the same character. You've always been.

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:29.970
You don't gain experience.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.530
And I feel like that's one thing that will has going for it.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:38.910
It also in terms of exploration has pretty locked ideas, at least in the beginning, right?

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:40.550
Like you can only go north.

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:43.850
They tell you that the next thing to do is north.

00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:45.130
You go north.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:54.070
And then afterwards, they maybe introduce the idea of branching paths where it's like you can go east or west, but it's not like you can go east and then north, south and west.

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:58.990
You know, it's like after that, you kind of are like, that's the next thing that I have to do.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:07.730
Or if I went the opposite direction because I didn't listen to anybody in the town, I'll get punished for it maybe by some strong enemies or maybe there will just not be anything to do there yet for me.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:19.750
But they don't completely let you just walk around the entire map without your sword and have no way to do anything and then be like, well, how the hell do I even get back to the beginning?

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:21.730
That problem never occurs.

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:30.270
Yeah, yeah. And, you know, to clarify, you know, what I was saying there, I guess I don't just mean as far as navigating the map.

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:38.130
I guess I mean other games that we've played, they're similar to this, whether it's like Faxanadu, which is kind of similar or or even Zelda 2.

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:47.890
You know, these are both different, but they have like a similar kind of goal to it where you're where you're exploring and in this like large story based game.

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:53.510
Those games, there was always times where I felt like I didn't know where to go, but I didn't know what to do next.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:10:00.870
This game has a does a good job of like letting you understand the layout of the world, but also letting you understand this is your goal.

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:02.450
This is where you should be trying to go.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:07.410
So I won't say it never happened where I got like lost, but almost never.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:12.250
And that probably comes down to the fact that there's minimal flavor in the dialogue.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:19.630
And what I mean by that is that they're being pretty clear about what you need to do depending on the person you talk to.

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:30.710
There's very little like, you know, oh, I wonder what they mean by that or, you know, or just like, oh, this is just somebody's building the story of this town.

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:33.450
Like this person is just explaining what happened in this town.

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:35.690
And now I have some world building for the most part.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:45.090
Characters in this game are really just telling you about items you'll later get or who you should speak to or where you should go, which is helpful, right?

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:54.110
I'd say that there there's still flavor and there are like a couple like huts per town where you'll get just like, oh, no, the evil.

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:59.810
What's a Bob that they took my they took my chickens or something along those lines.

