00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:42.410
Yeah, I mean, I agree that it's never that there is flavor to it.

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:49.170
But I do think that it is that there is substance there just as far as directing you where to go, which.

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:51.150
So I guess I agree with both of you.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:52.830
Yeah, exactly. It's effective.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:12:04.010
And it well, as I was playing it, I was like, it kind of got me thinking like, wait, what about what is it about this game that suddenly we're capable of having multiple full paragraphs for all these characters?

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:13.910
Whereas like something, you know, we had like Castlevania 2 or like Zelda 2 where it's like, oh, they had to they had to fit in what they were trying to say in like in like seven words or something.

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:15.270
And that's where everything got confusing.

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:17.890
That comes down to presentation, right, Joe?

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:30.910
I mean, when you talk to somebody, you enter a different kind of cut scene where, you know, the actual graphical sprites and characters are a much, much smaller section of the screen to your benefits.

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:32.250
