I'm obviously not an NES developer either, but I think what I was trying to say is just that, you know, there is a certain amount of like capabilities with the within like the screen.

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:50.690
And so I know for like Kirby's Adventure, a game that we'll get to sometime on this podcast, they actually like to to make it so that they could do more with the NES hardware.

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:56.610
They, you know, they made the actual like real estate of what happens in gameplay much smaller.

