01:01:31.570 --> 01:01:34.090
Uh, Willow is a complete package,

01:01:34.690 --> 01:01:36.650
and, while it might be simple,

01:01:36.890 --> 01:01:38.330
and I, you know, I use that word a lot,

01:01:38.470 --> 01:01:39.490
simple, straightforward,

01:01:39.930 --> 01:01:40.810
you know, even,

01:01:41.070 --> 01:01:44.370
uh, not that I want,

01:01:44.490 --> 01:01:45.590
like, Castlevania 2,

01:01:45.870 --> 01:01:47.590
like, what the fuck is that guy telling me?

01:01:47.710 --> 01:01:48.630
Like, I like that they're

01:01:48.630 --> 01:01:49.530
being clear about it.

01:01:49.570 --> 01:01:51.130
I also don't mind,

01:01:51.590 --> 01:01:52.530
you know, puzzles,

01:01:52.550 --> 01:01:53.650
and, uh,

01:01:53.930 --> 01:01:55.150
and rumors, and,

01:01:55.630 --> 01:01:57.090
uh, exploration, encouragement.

01:01:57.190 --> 01:01:58.270
I don't need them

01:01:58.270 --> 01:01:59.130
to necessarily, like,

01:01:59.170 --> 01:02:00.050
tell me where I'm going next.

01:02:00.070 --> 01:02:00.930
But even though it's

01:02:00.930 --> 01:02:02.390
a very simple and straightforward game,

01:02:02.570 --> 01:02:03.870
it gets everything

01:02:03.870 --> 01:02:05.250
that it sets out to do

01:02:05.250 --> 01:02:06.590
right. So,

01:02:06.630 --> 01:02:08.850
at worst, this game just isn't

01:02:08.850 --> 01:02:10.210
respectful of your time,

01:02:10.810 --> 01:02:12.270
uh, not in, like, the grinding thing,

01:02:12.350 --> 01:02:13.490
because I never really ran into that.

01:02:13.610 --> 01:02:15.030
Joe mentioned that that might be a problem later.

01:02:15.310 --> 01:02:16.490
But not respectful of your time

01:02:16.490 --> 01:02:18.630
in the sense of, like, you don't have a map,

01:02:18.690 --> 01:02:20.190
and sometimes you might go in the wrong direction,

01:02:20.330 --> 01:02:21.870
and then you gotta, like, backtrack a little bit.

01:02:22.090 --> 01:02:24.010
But what modern game,

01:02:24.250 --> 01:02:26.330
or modern 50-plus hour game,

01:02:26.370 --> 01:02:27.210
this game's only probably

01:02:27.210 --> 01:02:28.630
about five hours long,

01:02:28.650 --> 01:02:29.970
if you know what you're doing, uh,

01:02:30.230 --> 01:02:31.830
what modern 50-plus hour game

01:02:32.310 --> 01:02:34.090
doesn't, like, also waste your time

01:02:34.090 --> 01:02:35.250
a little bit here and there?

01:02:35.390 --> 01:02:36.430
Uh, I don't really think that

01:02:36.430 --> 01:02:37.370
that's, like, the end of the world.

01:02:37.370 --> 01:02:39.570
And when I look at, like, the current Essential Games list,

01:02:39.790 --> 01:02:40.670
I think it'd be a mistake

01:02:40.670 --> 01:02:41.890
not to have Willow on there,

01:02:41.990 --> 01:02:43.050
at least for now, uh,

01:02:43.190 --> 01:02:44.550
because I really enjoyed my time with it,

01:02:44.590 --> 01:02:45.570
and I think, again,

01:02:45.710 --> 01:02:47.070
everything it set out to do,

01:02:47.150 --> 01:02:48.710
it did. It just probably left

01:02:48.710 --> 01:02:49.870
a little, uh,

01:02:50.090 --> 01:02:51.190
more to desire.

01:02:51.190 --> 01:02:52.150
And just to further,

01:02:52.350 --> 01:02:54.310
like, go over the point of

01:02:54.890 --> 01:02:55.850
that we were singing

01:02:55.850 --> 01:02:57.170
its praises, and even just,

01:02:57.270 --> 01:02:58.110
like, trying to look at,

01:02:58.170 --> 01:02:59.550
like, well, what was negative reception

01:02:59.550 --> 01:03:00.550
like back in the day?

01:03:01.170 --> 01:03:03.130
And, uh, this magazine,

01:03:03.690 --> 01:03:04.990
Video Games and Computer Entertainment

01:03:04.990 --> 01:03:07.210
Magazine, gave it a 7 out of 10,

01:03:07.370 --> 01:03:08.510
praising the graphics,

01:03:08.790 --> 01:03:10.110
but was critical of the music

01:03:10.110 --> 01:03:12.250
and the complex password system.

01:03:12.430 --> 01:03:13.510
It's like, maybe,

01:03:13.690 --> 01:03:15.030
maybe those are problems,

01:03:15.090 --> 01:03:16.630
but come on, you're gonna detract

01:03:16.630 --> 01:03:17.610
three points for

01:03:17.610 --> 01:03:18.510
some music,

01:03:18.510 --> 01:03:20.730
which personally, not the worst music

01:03:20.730 --> 01:03:21.950
I've ever heard in video games.

01:03:22.210 --> 01:03:23.270
Honestly, some of it was probably

01:03:23.270 --> 01:03:24.610
pretty good. I don't remember it that much,

01:03:24.670 --> 01:03:26.170
so it couldn't be bad if I don't remember it.

01:03:26.410 --> 01:03:27.510
But password systems

01:03:27.510 --> 01:03:28.350
get a pass,

01:03:28.510 --> 01:03:30.910
right? I do remember

01:03:30.910 --> 01:03:31.730
some of the tracks.

01:03:31.930 --> 01:03:33.130
I did like, uh,

01:03:33.390 --> 01:03:34.850
some of them. Some of them also,

01:03:35.010 --> 01:03:36.630
though, are kind of repetitive

01:03:36.630 --> 01:03:38.210
over time. Um,

01:03:38.630 --> 01:03:39.890
but just on your point

01:03:39.890 --> 01:03:40.730
about the,

01:03:40.910 --> 01:03:42.470
uh, password systems,

01:03:42.690 --> 01:03:44.770
I think that's just, that was a priority

01:03:44.770 --> 01:03:45.850
for some people.

01:03:46.050 --> 01:03:47.950
Like, if it's completely unwieldy

01:03:47.950 --> 01:03:49.210
to be able to

01:03:49.210 --> 01:03:50.630
continue your progress,

01:03:50.870 --> 01:03:52.130
like, I think that's a big

01:03:52.130 --> 01:03:54.350
deal for people

01:03:54.350 --> 01:03:55.350
that aren't, like,

01:03:55.350 --> 01:03:56.570
that didn't have, like, a smartphone

01:03:56.570 --> 01:03:57.630
to take a picture

01:03:57.630 --> 01:03:58.510
of something or,

01:03:58.510 --> 01:03:59.830
uh, any other

01:04:00.790 --> 01:04:01.850
possibly less than

01:04:01.850 --> 01:04:03.350
gray market legal way

01:04:03.350 --> 01:04:04.790
to play a game without having to

01:04:04.790 --> 01:04:05.590
write down a password.

01:04:05.990 --> 01:04:07.590
So, I think it's just

01:04:07.590 --> 01:04:09.250
a matter of modern priorities.

01:04:10.350 --> 01:04:11.370
Yeah, I agree.

01:04:11.730 --> 01:04:12.550
Uh, because I don't even

01:04:12.550 --> 01:04:13.730
remember the password. I think the password

01:04:13.730 --> 01:04:14.650
is, like, 12 digits.

01:04:15.210 --> 01:04:16.670
So you can write that down in a couple seconds.

01:04:16.870 --> 01:04:17.750
18. Oh, 18.

01:04:17.870 --> 01:04:19.670
That's a lot. But,

01:04:19.710 --> 01:04:21.070
uh, but I will say that,

01:04:21.130 --> 01:04:22.070
yeah, I was going to mention,

01:04:22.090 --> 01:04:23.050
I forgot too, that, like,

01:04:23.050 --> 01:04:24.070
another thing that I would,

01:04:24.110 --> 01:04:25.450
like, give a minor negative

01:04:25.450 --> 01:04:26.510
is that, like, I wish there was

01:04:26.510 --> 01:04:28.110
a little more music variety in this game

01:04:28.110 --> 01:04:28.950
as well. It's like,

01:04:29.070 --> 01:04:30.590
it's like there's, like, one track that's,

01:04:30.630 --> 01:04:31.810
like, a lot of the overworld

01:04:31.810 --> 01:04:33.750
theme and then switches to a battle track

01:04:33.750 --> 01:04:35.210
